      "rerank_score_norm": 0.31189319116489467,
      "final_score": 0.5919630883541773,
      "text": "Raoul Daoust, MD, MSc, Emergency Department, Hôpital du Sacré-­ Coeur de Montréal, 5400 Gouin Blvd. West, Montreal, Québec H4J 1C5, Canada. Email: raoul.daoust@umontreal.ca Background: Opioids are often prescribed for acute pain to patients discharged from the emergency department (ED), but there is a paucity of data on their short-­ term use. The purpose of this study was to synthesize the evidence regarding the efficacy of prescribed opioids compared to nonopioid analgesics for acute pain relief in ED-­ discharged patients.",
